{ This system has been around for ages, but it experienced a boost in popularity when Magnus Carlsen used it to clinch his World Championship match against Sergey Karjakin. Not long after that, I managed to win a nice game against Harikrishna with Black. Amongst club players and amateurs too, this system keeps popping up every now and again, as White players try to surprise their opponents. The idea is to keep the knight on b1 for now and get the Maroczy bind with c4. Chess, however, is a game of tempi and it is now Black to move. }
